        "original_id": "5af2d51f-b9f8-559c-9269-9aa60ff95719",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Orlando Brown, Raven-Symoné, Anneliese van der Pol, Kyla Pratt\n- TV series: Family Matters, That's So Raven, Major Payne, Two of a Kind, Waynehead, Max Keeble's Big Move, Eddie's Million Dollar Cook Off, Perfect Strangers\n- Groups: Disney Channel Circle of Stars\n- Places: Chicago, Illinois\n- Roles: Eddie Thomas, 3J Winslow, Tiger, Max, Damey Wayne, Dobbs, Frankie\n\nFacts:\n- Family Matters aired on ABC from September 22, 1989 to May 9, 1997, and then aired on CBS from September 19, 1997 to July 17, 1998.\n- Family Matters is a spin-off of Perfect Strangers and follows the Winslow family, a middle-class African American family living in Chicago, Illinois.\n- Orlando Brown was born on December 4, 1987, and is an American actor, voice actor, rapper, and singer.\n- Orlando Brown is best known for playing Eddie Thomas in That's So Raven, 3J Winslow in Family Matters, Tiger in Major Payne, Max in Two of a Kind, Damey Wayne in Waynehead, Dobbs in Max Keeble's Big Move, and Frankie in Eddie's Million Dollar Cook Off.\n- Orlando Brown, Raven-Symoné, Anneliese van der Pol, and Kyla Pratt were part of the original line-up of Disney Channel Circle of Stars.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "645f940e-b5f2-50bc-a702-72ad0d54f87f",
        "text": "Page: Orlando Brown (actor). Sentence: Orlando Brown (born December 4, 1987) is an American actor, voice actor, rapper and singer.\nPage: Orlando Brown (actor). Sentence: He is best known for his role as Eddie Thomas in \"That's So Raven\", 3J Winslow in \"Family Matters\", Tiger in \"Major Payne\", Max in \"Two of a Kind\", Damey Wayne in the short-lived Waynehead, Dobbs in \"Max Keeble's Big Move\", and Frankie in \"Eddie's Million Dollar Cook Off\".\nPage: Family Matters. Sentence: Family Matters is an American sitcom which originated on ABC from September 22, 1989 to May 9, 1997, before moving to CBS from September 19, 1997 to July 17, 1998.\nPage: Family Matters. Sentence: A spin-off of \"Perfect Strangers,\" the series revolves around the Winslow family, a middle-class African American family living in Chicago, Illinois.\nPage: Disney Channel Circle of Stars. Sentence: A group of actors and actresses who have appeared in Disney Channel television series and original movies, including Raven-Symoné, Orlando Brown, Anneliese van der Pol, and Kyla Pratt, were all part of the original line-up.",
